  "result": "I added `click.KeyValue`, and `python -m pytest tests/test_types.py -q` passes (47 passed, 2 skipped). I didn't run the full suite.\n\n- **Class:** `KeyValue` is a `ParamType` subclass in `src/click/types.py`, placed right after `UUIDParameterType`. It splits on the first `=` only, so `a=b=c` gives `(\"a\", \"b=c\")` and `a=` gives `(\"a\", \"\")`.\n- **Errors:** input with no `=` or an empty key calls `self.fail(...)` with `'\u2026' is not a valid key=value pair.`\n- **Export:** the class itself, not an instance, is exported from `src/click/__init__.py`.\n- **Tests:** two parametrized tests in `tests/test_types.py` cover the valid cases above and the failures `abc`, `=value` and an empty string (exit code 2 plus the error message).\n- **Already-parsed tuples:** `convert()` also returns a tuple unchanged. You didn't ask for this; I added it to match how `UUIDParameterType` accepts an already-converted `uuid.UUID`, for example from a default.",
